# Build context = image content: the Dockerfile copies the whole context, so this
# deny-list is the ONLY thing deciding what ships. Keep the "never ship" section
# first and exhaustive; anything not listed here ends up in the image.
#
# `supabase` and `scripts` were excluded here until now, which meant the image
# physically could not run its own migrations — the migrate service loads
# supabase/migrations/*.sql through core/migrate.py. They must stay in.

# --- Never ship: secrets and key material (CLAUDE.md §4.6/§4.7) --------------
# `.env.*` also covers `.env.example`: nothing in the image reads it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
secrets/

# --- Never ship: history, CI config, agent config ----------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# --- Not needed to serve the control API or to migrate -----------------------
# The console is built and deployed separately. `tests` matters most here:
# tests/fixtures/ holds the local auth shim and generated key material, none of
# which belongs in a runtime image (Story 1.9 AC3). deploy/auth_compat.sql is
# the production counterpart of that shim, and it DOES ship.
frontend
tests
docs
**/*.md

# --- Build/test artefacts (host-specific, never valid inside the image) ------
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
htmlcov
coverage.xml
.coverage
.next
node_modules
